You are implementing the Company Post Service for a talent marketplace platform.

This service is similar to the Community Service feed, but it serves job recruitment posts from companies.

The system allows users to:

View job posts

View post details

Save posts

See whether a post is saved

Your task is to implement the service layer and repository logic.

Follow the same architecture used in the Community Service.

Database Schema
COMPANY_POST
Column	Type
postId (PK)	int
companyId (FK)	int
position	nvarchar
address	nvarchar
salary	nvarchar
employmentType	enum
experienceYear	int
quantity	int
jobDescription	nvarchar
requirementsMandatory	nvarchar
requirementsPreferred	nvarchar
benefits	nvarchar
createAt	datetime
status	int

Status meaning:

1 = active
0 = deleted
2 = hidden
COMPANY_POST_MEDIA

Stores media attached to the job post.

Column	Type
id (PK)	int
companyPostId (FK)	int
type	nvarchar (image / video)
name	nvarchar
address	nvarchar (media url)

Each post can have multiple media items.

COMPANY_POST_SAVE

Stores saved posts by users.

Column	Type
id (PK)	int
companyPostId (FK)	int
userId (FK)	int

Rules:

1 user can save many posts
1 post can be saved by many users

Recommended constraint:

UNIQUE(userId, companyPostId)
COMPLIMENT

(Not directly used in feed)

Column	Type
id (PK)	int
portfolioId (FK)	int
companyId (FK)	int
state	int
content	nvarchar
API 1: Get Job Post Feed
Endpoint
GET /api/company/posts

Query parameters:

cursor
limit

Example:

GET /api/company/posts?cursor=20&limit=10
Feed Response
[
  {
    "postId": 1,
    "position": "Senior UX Designer",
    "companyName": "Google Inc.",
    "companyAvatar": "url",
    "mediaType": "image",
    "mediaUrl": "url",
    "address": "Hồ Chí Minh",
    "salary": "25.000.000 - 30.000.000",
    "employmentType": "Full-time",
    "isSaved": true
  }
]
Feed Query Logic

Tables used:

COMPANY_POST
JOIN COMPANY
LEFT JOIN COMPANY_POST_MEDIA
LEFT JOIN COMPANY_POST_SAVE

Rules:

Only active posts
WHERE COMPANY_POST.status = 1
Pagination (Cursor Based)
WHERE postId < @cursor
ORDER BY postId DESC
LIMIT @limit
Media selection

A post may contain many media items.

For the feed, return only the first media.

Example SQL logic:

SELECT TOP 1 *
FROM COMPANY_POST_MEDIA
WHERE companyPostId = postId
ORDER BY id ASC
Saved state

Determine if user saved the post.

isSaved =
EXISTS(
 SELECT 1
 FROM COMPANY_POST_SAVE
 WHERE userId = @userId
 AND companyPostId = postId
)
